#
# NEVER FOR A RELEASE (the release job refuses a build with this option on).
# An overlay on sdkconfig.defaults for a first boot with a new receiver: the
# station's first configuration of the receiver waits for the user.
#
#   idf.py -B build-hold -D SDKCONFIG=build-hold/sdkconfig \
#          -D "SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS=sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.hold" build
#
# On a device whose receiver profile was never applied, the first boot
# writes gnss/autocfg = 0, gnss/recovery = 2 (alerts only, if unset) and
# gnss/hold = 1 before anything reaches the receiver. Until the user
# confirms the apply on the receiver page (or in the setup wizard), only
# queries are sent. The hold stays in NVS, so flashing the station build
# afterwards keeps it until the user applies. In QEMU:
# tools/qemu/run.sh --overlay sdkconfig.hold (builds into build-qemu-hold/).

CONFIG_STATION_HOLD_FIRST_APPLY=y
